                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Please split into afterXXX + std::bind_front.\nNested lambda violates COMMON_ERRORS.md \u00a714:\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/master/docs/COMMON_ERRORS.md#14-very-long-lambda-callbacks"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/fabric.hpp",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "Done.\nThe outer lambda is now the free function `afterGetSwitchPowerStateService()` and the inner one is `afterGetSwitchPowerState()`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/fabric.hpp",
                    "line": 58,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Please classify ec instead of silently swallowing all errors"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/fabric.hpp",
                    "line": 58,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "Done."
